# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in every working tree.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout converts text files to CRLF (Git for Windows
# defaults core.autocrlf to true), which makes `prettier --check` fail on every
# file, breaks the renderer's byte-exact HTML assertions, and corrupts the
# shebang handling of the shell scripts. CI runs on Windows, so this is load
# bearing rather than tidiness.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched: these are binary regardless of what Git guesses.
*.wasm binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz binary

# Generated. Collapsed in diffs and reviews, and never merged by hand.
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true -diff
